    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0508" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/764</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Ministry of Foreign
                            Affairs at Nanking to the Chinese
                            Legation</hi><anchor n="58" xml:id="d417-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-10">December 10, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Minister Chian[g] at Tokyo
                    reported that the Soviet Ambassador informed him that General Su Ping-Wen was
                    permitted to depart <pb facs="0509" n="411" xml:id="pg411"/> while large number
                    of soldiers were willing to remain in the Union of Socialist Soviet Republics,
                    thus confirming Tass report.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d417-f1" n="58" type="source" xml:id="d417-f1-content">
                <p>Copy of telegram transmitted to the Department by the Chinese Legation, December
                    10, 1932.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
